## Functional Failure Conditions

| Failure Condition ID | Function | Failure Condition |
|----------------------|----------|-------------------|
| FC-001 | Navigator Selection | Active navigator state is ambiguous to the pilot |
| FC-002 | FMS2 Control | FMS2 does not provide functional parity with FMS1 in independent navigator mode |
| FC-003 | CDI Source Selection | CDI function is unavailable or inconsistent for FMS2 workflows |
| FC-004 | Cursor Mode Control | Cursor mode is active but not clearly annunciated |
| FC-005 | Map Range Control | Map zoom/range control is unavailable for one navigator |
| FC-006 | Map Pan Control | Map pan behavior is unavailable or inconsistent |
| FC-007 | Shift Mode Control | Shift mode is active but not clearly indicated |
| FC-008 | Mode Annunciation | Controller mode state is not visible to the pilot |
| FC-009 | Architecture Profile Selection | Controller uses integrated avionics assumptions while operating independent navigators |
| FC-010 | Control Allocation | High-frequency IFR functions require shifted inputs unnecessarily |



## FHA Assessment Table

| Function ID | Function | Failure Condition | Potential Operational Effect | Recommended Mitigation |
|------------|----------|-------------------|------------------------------|------------------------|
| F-001 | Navigator Selection | Active navigator state is ambiguous | Pilot may apply inputs to the wrong navigator or spend additional time verifying state | Provide clear FMS1/FMS2 annunciation |
| F-002 | FMS1 Control | Primary navigator function unavailable | Reduced usability of primary avionics interface | Maintain complete FMS1 function mapping |
| F-003 | FMS2 Control | FMS2 lacks parity with FMS1 | Increased workload and reduced independent navigator usability | Provide full FMS2 parity in Independent Navigator Mode |
| F-004 | CDI Source Selection | CDI unavailable or inconsistent on FMS2 | Reduced workflow consistency and possible navigation source confusion | Implement CDI behavior for FMS2 where supported |
| F-005 | Cursor Mode Control | Cursor mode active without annunciation | Mode awareness degradation and possible incorrect knob input | Add cursor mode LED/state feedback |
| F-006 | Map Range Control | Map zoom unavailable for FMS2 | Increased heads-down time and reduced map usability | Implement Shift + FMS2 Pan/Zoom mode |
| F-007 | Map Pan Control | Pan behavior unavailable or inconsistent | Reduced map review capability | Add optional pan mode using existing controls |
| F-008 | Shift Mode Control | Shift mode active without clear indication | Increased likelihood of mode confusion | Blink selected mode LED while shift is active |
| F-009 | Mode Annunciation | Active state not visible | Pilot must verify state through trial, memory, or display inspection | Expose and drive LED states for active modes |
| F-010 | Architecture Profile Selection | Wrong architecture model applied | Functional mismatch between controller behavior and avionics design | Add Integrated Avionics Mode and Independent Navigator Mode |



## Effects by Architecture Type

| Failure Condition | Integrated Avionics Effect | Independent Navigator Effect |
|------------------|----------------------------|------------------------------|
| FMS2 functional asymmetry | May be acceptable if FMS2 represents an MFD | Not acceptable because FMS2 represents a second navigator |
| CDI unavailable on FMS2 | May be acceptable in G1000-style workflows | Creates functional inconsistency in dual navigator workflows |
| Shift state not annunciated | Increases workload | Increases workload and may affect independent navigator control |
| Cursor state not annunciated | Increases verification burden | May reduce confidence in FMS2 map/cursor operation |
| Pan/Zoom unavailable on FMS2 | May be acceptable depending on display role | Reduces independent map control for Navigator 2 |



## Qualitative Effect Categories

This assessment does not assign formal certification-level severity classifications.

Instead, effects are described using qualitative operational categories.

| Category | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Usability Impact | Function is harder to use but does not prevent task completion |
| Workload Impact | Function increases cognitive or physical workload |
| Mode Awareness Impact | Function creates uncertainty about active controller state |
| Workflow Impact | Function disrupts expected pilot workflow |
| Training Transferability Impact | Function reduces similarity between simulator workflow and real cockpit workflow |



